.TH LINUXCNCTOP\-UI "1"  "2026-07-31" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
linuxcnctop\-ui \- the LinuxCNC status window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxcnctop\-ui
[\fI\-\-url URL\fR] [\fI\-\-title TITLE\fR] [\fI\-\-width W\fR] [\fI\-\-height H\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlinuxcnctop\-ui\fR opens the LinuxCNC status window: one row per status
field, with recently changed values highlighted. Above the list are a filter
box (matching both field names and values), the update rate, a Freeze button, a
raw\-JSON view and Copy All.

It is a \fBgmcui\fR(1) symlink onto the \fIlinuxcnctop\fR web application, which
the running controller serves at \fI/app/linuxcnctop/\fR \(em the same page can
be opened in any browser. The server comes from \fB$GMC_REST_URL\fR (default
http://127.0.0.1:5080) and the task instance from \fB$GMC_INSTANCE\fR (default
\fImilltask\fR).

Lengths are displayed in millimetres, the unit the controller keeps internally,
regardless of the machine's configured units.

This is the command AXIS runs for Machine > Show LinuxCNC Status. From a
terminal, prefer \fBlinuxcnctop\fR(1): it opens this window by default and adds
a text mode for headless use. Unlike \fBlinuxcnctop\fR, this command rejects
arguments it does not recognise, including the legacy \fB\-ini\fR \fIINIFILE\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR
Server URL, overriding \fB$GMC_REST_URL\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR
Window title.
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fIW\fR, \fB\-\-height\fR \fIH\fR
Initial window size in pixels.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GMC_REST_URL
Base URL of the controller's REST API.
.TP
.B GMC_INSTANCE
Task instance to display.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBlinuxcnctop(1)\fR, \fBgmcui(1)\fR, \fBLinuxCNC(1)\fR

Much more information about LinuxCNC and HAL is available in the LinuxCNC
and HAL User Manuals, found at /usr/share/doc/LinuxCNC/.

